# §9 operators + value-type methods
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ENTERS (docs/design/plano-secao9-operadores-e-value-type-methods.md):
#   - THE VALUE-TYPE BODY AST, in `src/parser/ast.tks`: a new `NewtypeBody` (a prim-backed value-type
#     WITH a body — nominal, non-transparent), `methods` fields on `EnumBody`/`FlagsBody`, and an
#     `is_operator` flag on `Function` (all empty/false on every existing node — fixpoint-inert). The
#     `.tkb` codec (`src/emit/tkb_*.tks`) serializes the new node/fields in parity.
#   - PARSER, in `src/parser/parse_decl.tks`: `parse_value_type_members` parses the trailing
#     `{ method-or-operator* }` block of `type X = <prim> { … }` / `enum … { … }` / `flags … { … }`;
#     `operator` is CONTEXTUAL (precedent `trait` — an `Ident("operator")` followed by a dunder name),
#     so no reserved token is added. A field/const/static member is a precise located parse error
#     (ruling 10).
#   - CHECKER, in `src/checker/collect.tks` / `src/checker/typer.tks`:
#       * value-type instance methods collect + dispatch through the existing method machinery; the
#         flags method honest-stop is lifted; a `self` operand/return type resolves to the owner.
#       * `check_operator_invariants` validates each operator at DEFINITION (rulings 1/3/4/5): dunder
#         name, arity, at least one `self` operand, the class-mandated return (arith/bitwise → self,
#         comparison → bool, index → element), `__index` only on an indexed carrier, and the mandatory
#         comparator counterparts (__eq⟂__ne, __lt⟂__ge, __gt⟂__le).
#       * the operator dunder lookup (`dunder_of_binop`/`value_op_owner`/`dispatch_binop_operator`),
#         gated so it fires only when at least one operand is a NAMED value-type (ruling 7), lowers a
#         matched operator to a static `Owner::__dunder(l, r)` call and otherwise reduces each operand
#         to its base (rulings 8), across `type_binary`/`type_unary`/`type_compare`/`type_index`.
#       * E9 (ruling 9): `value_type_base`/`value_type_reduce` reduce a nominal newtype to its backing
#         so `type_cast` treats newtype<->base as a representation no-op, exactly like the enum<->int
#         (E7) and flags<->int (E8) paths.
#   - BACKENDS: `src/codegen/codegen.tks` lowers a `NewtypeBody` to a C typedef of its backing machine
#     type; `src/lir/lower.tks` records a value-type carrier in the LEnumInfo table (`find_value_carrier`)
#     so the native backend lowers a value-type to its backing machine class. Both are corpus-inert (no
#     `NewtypeBody` exists in the compiler's own sources).
#
# ACCEPT fixture (examples/regressions/value_type_operators): arithmetic with both dispatch legs,
# comparison + counterpart, a readonly method on an enum and on a flags value-type, and operator
# __index over a []i32-backed newtype — each extracting/reconstructing through the E9 cast. REJECT
